  "id": "affective-assessment",
  "term": "affective assessment",
  "definition": "Affective assessment is the evaluation of a person’s emotional state or changes in emotion during an interaction. In this context, it refers to judging a child’s feelings during a forensic interview by using cues such as nonverbal behavior or vocal emotion patterns, sometimes with AI as a supplementary aid rather than a replacement for professional judgment.",
